{"n": 145, "w": 1000, "h": 1286, "img": "145.webp", "text": "102 Suspension and steering systems\n\nTorque wrench settings\n\nFront suspension\nStrut damper rod nut\nRod with external hexagon\nRod with internal hexagon\nStrut cartridge threaded collar .\nStrut upper mounting nuts . . .\nFront control arm (3-Series)\nControl arm-to-steering knuckle balljoint nut\nControl arm-to-subframe balljoint nut\nControl arm bush bracket bolts ..\nLower control arm (5-Series)\n\nControl arm-to-steering arm balljoint stud nut .\n\nControl arm pivot bolt\nThrust arm (5-Series)\nThrust arm-to-steering arm balljoint stud nut\nThrust arm through-bolt .\nFront hub (wheel bearing) nut .\nSteering arm-to-strut bolts (5-Series)\nAnti-roll bar (3-Series)\nAnti-roll bar-to-connecting link bolt\nAnti-roll bar mounting brackets-to-subframe\nConnecting link-to-bracket\nConnecting link bracket-to-control arm .\nAnti-roll bar (5-Series)\nAnti-roll bar mounting brackets\nAnti-roll bar link-to-strut housing locknut\nYellow chrome .\nWhite chrome\nYellow\n\n1 General information\n\nWarning: Whenever any of the\nsuspension or steering fasteners\nare loosened or removed, they\nmust be inspected and if\n\nnecessary, new ones fitted, of the same\n\npart number or of original-equipment\nquality and design. Torque specifications\nmust be followed for proper reassembly\nand component retention. Never attempt\nto heat, straighten or weld any suspension\nor steering component. Any bent or\ndamaged parts must be renewed.\n\nThe front suspension (see illustrations) is a\nMacPherson strut design. The struts are\nsecured at the upper ends to reinforced areas\nat the top of the wheel arches, and at the\nlower ends to the steering arms/control arms.\nAn anti-roll bar is attached to the control arms\nvia connecting links, and to the suspension\nsubframe (3-Series models) or the underbody\n(5-Series models).\n\nThe independent rear suspension system\non 3-Series models (see illustration) features\ncoil springs and telescopic shock absorbers.\nThe upper ends of the shock absorbers are\nattached to the body; the lower ends are\nconnected to trailing arms. An anti-roll bar is\nattached to the trailing arms via links, and to\nthe body with clamps.\n\nThe independent rear suspension system on\n5-Series models (see illustration) uses coil-\n\nNm Torque wrench settings Nm\nRear suspension\nRear shock absorber (3-Series)\n65 Shock absorber-to-upper mounting bracket . 12 to 15\n44 Shock absorber-to-trailing arm 71 to 85\n130 Rear shock absorber (5-Series)\n22 Lower mounting bolt 125 to 142\nUpper mounting nut . 22 to 24\n64 Upper spring mounting-to-shock absorber locknut .. 22 to 24\n83 iling arms (3-Series)\n4 ling arm-to-lower mounting 71 to 85\nling arm-to-anti-roll bar . . 22 to 23\n85 Trailing arms (5-Series)\n77 Trailing arm-to-rear axle carrier (rubber bush\nthrough-bolt and nut) 66\n85 Trailing arm-to-axle carrier connecting link (1983-on) ... 126\n130 Rear wheel bearing drive flange a axle nut n- Series)\n290 M22. . : 175 to 210\nvooteeeee 65 M27. 235 to 260\n4\n22 Steering system\n22 Steering wheel retaining nut 79\n4 Steering column universal joint pinch-bolt . . . 22\nSteering gear-to-subframe mounting bolts (3-Series) . 4\nbeveee eee 22 Steering box-to-front suspension subframe bolts (5-Series) 42\nTrack rod end-to-steering arm nut . . 7\n20 Track rod end clamping bolt......... 14\n33 Pitman arm-to-steering box (5-Series) . 140\n58 Steering linkage balljoints (all) ..... 0.00... 0... e eee 37\n\nover shock absorber units instead of separate\nshock absorbers and coil springs. The upper\nends are attached to the body; the lower ends\nare connected to the trailing arms. The rear\nsuspension of 5-Series models is otherwise\nsimilar to that of 3-Series models: two trailing\narms connected by an anti-roll bar.\n\nThe steering system consists of the\nsteering wheel, a steering column, a universal\njoint shaft, the steering gear, the power\n\nsteering pump (where fitted) and the steering\nlinkage, which connects the steering gear to\nthe steering arms. On 3-Series models, a\nrack-and-pinion steering gear is attached\ndirectly to the steering arms via the track rods\nand track rod ends. On 5-Series models, a\nrecirculating-ball steering box is connected to\nthe steering arms via a Pitman arm, a centre\ntrack rod, the outer track rods and the track\nrod ends.\n\n1.1a Front suspension and steering components (3-Series models)\n\n1 Subframe\n2 Anti-roll bar\n\n3 Anti-roll bar link\n4 Control arm\n\n5 Strut\n6 Track rod end\n\n7 Steering gear", "words": [["102", 0.0683, 0.0369, 0.1058, 0.048], ["Suspension", 0.1175, 0.0363, 0.2125, 0.0506], ["and", 0.22, 0.0369, 0.2492, 0.048], ["steering", 0.2558, 0.0369, 0.32, 0.0506], ["systems", 0.3275, 0.0376, 0.3942, 0.0506], ["Torque", 0.0667, 0.0771, 0.1233, 0.0901], ["wrench", 0.1283, 0.0771, 0.1867, 0.0875], ["settings", 0.1933, 0.0771, 0.2558, 0.0901], ["Front", 0.0675, 0.0992, 0.1008, 0.1069], ["suspension", 0.105, 0.0992, 0.1767, 0.1095], ["Strut", 0.0675, 0.1134, 0.0958, 0.1218], ["damper", 0.1, 0.1134, 0.1458, 0.1238], ["rod", 0.15, 0.1134, 0.1692, 0.1212], ["nut", 0.1742, 0.1141, 0.1925, 0.1212], ["Rod", 0.0967, 0.1257, 0.1192, 0.1335], ["with", 0.1242, 0.1257, 0.1483, 0.1335], ["external", 0.1533, 0.1257, 0.1992, 0.1342], ["hexagon", 0.205, 0.1257, 0.255, 0.1361], ["Rod", 0.0967, 0.138, 0.1192, 0.1458], ["with", 0.1242, 0.138, 0.1483, 0.1458], ["internal", 0.1533, 0.138, 0.1958, 0.1458], ["hexagon", 0.2008, 0.138, 0.2517, 0.1484], ["Strut", 0.0675, 0.151, 0.0958, 0.1594], ["cartridge", 0.1, 0.151, 0.1525, 0.1614], ["threaded", 0.1575, 0.151, 0.21, 0.1588], ["collar", 0.215, 0.151, 0.2467, 0.1588], [".", 0.2558, 0.1575, 0.2575, 0.1588], ["Strut", 0.0675, 0.1633, 0.0958, 0.1717], ["upper", 0.1, 0.1653, 0.1342, 0.1737], ["mounting", 0.1392, 0.1633, 0.1942, 0.1737], ["nuts", 0.1992, 0.164, 0.2242, 0.1717], [".", 0.2333, 0.1698, 0.235, 0.1711], [".", 0.2408, 0.1698, 0.2425, 0.1711], [".", 0.2483, 0.